      "writtenOn": "2023-08-11T06:37:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is strange to me that we use UncaughtExceptionHandler but didn\u0027t use\nits own mechanism to fire exception like: \nmHandlerThread.setUncaughtExceptionHandler(mDeps.getUncaughtExceptionHandler());\n\nIs it better if we use setUncaughtExceptionHandler instead of manually calling catchExceptionOnHandlerThread and invoking uncaughtException()?\nOr is there something I missed?",
