      "writtenOn": "2023-08-14T11:34:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The uncaught exception handler doesn\u0027t actually let the thread continue. The handler gets called, but the thread still terminates with the exception (it wouldn\u0027t know where to resume execution). In tests, that means the tests can\u0027t clean up because cleaning up involves waiting for the handler threads.\n\nBy contrast, this catches the exception but leaves the thread running, and processes the next message.\n\nThat\u0027s why this is necessary.",
      "parentUuid": "194caee1_5d37522b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5752,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 5752,
        "endChar": 58
