      "writtenOn": "2023-08-11T06:37:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Stuipid question: How do we prevent NC changes for other existing immutable capabilities e.g. NET_CAPABILITY_NOT_METERED? \n  If they are already enforced to be immutable, what is the reason we create this function?\n  Alternatively, if we did not do anything, can they also be applied here?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 441,
        "startChar": 79,
        "endLine": 441,
        "endChar": 85
      },
      "revId": "63a5dd87bfc89afa8ca3501c0bd05f730a77eb47",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a9319c98_316f941d",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/NetworkAgentInfo.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 441,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-14T11:34:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "• Originally, they were simply not enforced at all. That is the case for most immutable caps, like NOT_METERED or INTERNET.\n  → In fact, some OEMs actually do remove and add INTERNET dynamically although that is actually catastrophic for apps in some situations (and likely causes infinite loops in some cases on these devices).\n  → Note how because of that, we can never actually enforce these, because we\u0027d break the functionality they implemented in this incorrect way.\n\n• Later, we started ignoring changes that we couldn\u0027t make dynamically. This protects the system server, but it\u0027s very unhelpful to the network provider authors, because it just silently fails to take effect.\n → See `NetworkAgentInfo#getDeclaredCapabilitiesSanitized`, which resets the owner UID silently. Turns out Telephony had (still has ?) a bug where they tried to change this and didn\u0027t notice it wasn\u0027t reflected.\n → The reason we did this is because we couldn\u0027t crash the agent, since there is no place to do it. We could crash in NetworkAgent, but we\u0027d still need protection in the system server.\n\n• Because of the above, I now think it is really necessary to crash. If you try to mutate the LOCAL_NETWORK capability you\u0027ll mess up routing on the system. I just never want this to happen, and any network provider author trying to do it to notice for sure. Hence this new scheme. Our API is not the easiest to use, and I am tired of users misusing it without realizing. This gives us a very heavy hammer to prevent stuff that we really do not want.",
      "parentUuid": "370807ea_19f101fe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 441,
        "startChar": 79,
        "endLine": 441,
        "endChar": 85
      },
      "revId": "63a5dd87bfc89afa8ca3501c0bd05f730a77eb47",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
